SCRIPT 10c — Forest Zone Spatial Analysis Summary
========================================================================

1. SPATIAL PREDICTORS
----------------------------------------
   β₂ vs elevation: r = 0.981, R² = 0.963
   Elevation is the dominant predictor of β₂ (95.1% variance explained).
   Distance from ridge adds negligible information for β₂.
   β₃: elevation R² = 0.619, + dist_ridge R² = 0.739
   β₁: no strong spatial predictor (best: Easting r = 0.62)

2. CONTINUUM OR TWO GROUPS?
----------------------------------------
   C4 β₂ = 2.643 ± 0.479
   C5 β₂ = 1.208 ± 0.225
   t-test p = 0.0000 — two distinct groups.
   β₁ t-test p = 0.4472 — ranges overlap (not distinguishing).
   WMC3 (clearfell): β₁ = 2.406, β₂ = 1.842 — sits between C4 and C5.

3. OUTLIER ASSESSMENT
----------------------------------------
   NW10 (broadleaf): β₁ = 3.481 (C4 mean = 2.482), dist_ridge = 360 m
   Both position (closest to ridge) and canopy type may contribute.
   CEH14: β₂ = 3.723 at elev = 14.4 m — consistent with elevation trend,
   not a genuine outlier (upper end of tight linear relationship).

4. C4/C5 BOUNDARY
----------------------------------------
   C4 elevation: 8.7–14.4 m (n = 9)
   C5 elevation: 4.8–6.5 m (n = 5)
   Elevation gap: 2.2 m (zero overlap).
   C4 Northing: 363760–364488
   C5 Northing: 363533–363615
   Conclusion: boundary reflects a real topographic/substrate
   transition (dune ridge → coastal plain), not an arbitrary cut.
   Pearson affinity: 14/14 wells have best-match = assigned cluster.

  · Script 10c complete.


